From: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:30:46 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 17/28] virtio-msg: send required traffic on the
 must-deliver path

Add virtio_msg_bus_send_must_deliver() and use it for replies and
events that must eventually reach the peer.

This keeps required traffic on an explicit must-deliver path while
preserving the existing send() fallback for transports that do not
implement a dedicated callback.

With that fallback, virtio-msg-amp-pci still routes required-delivery
traffic through plain send() and therefore remains lossy under retryable
outbound FIFO backpressure. A transport-side follow-up is expected to
either implement send_must_deliver with receive-side retry preservation,
or explicitly document/accept the lossy behavior.

Signed-off-by: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-msg-bus.c         | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 hw/virtio/virtio-msg.c             | 30 +++++++++++++++---------------
 include/hw/virtio/virtio-msg-bus.h |  7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-msg-bus.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-msg-bus.c
index abf2218d9b21..4e968eb0323d 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-msg-bus.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-msg-bus.c
@@ -53,6 +53,24 @@ int virtio_msg_bus_send(BusState *bus, VirtIOMSG *msg_req)
     return r;
 }
 
+int virtio_msg_bus_send_must_deliver(BusState *bus, VirtIOMSG *msg_req)
+{
+    VirtIOMSGBusDevice *bd = virtio_msg_bus_get_device(bus);
+    VirtIOMSGBusDeviceClass *bdc;
+
+    if (!virtio_msg_bus_peer_ready(bd)) {
+        return VIRTIO_MSG_ERROR_RETRY;
+    }
+
+    bdc = VIRTIO_MSG_BUS_DEVICE_CLASS(object_get_class(OBJECT(bd)));
+
+    if (bdc->send_must_deliver) {
+        return bdc->send_must_deliver(bd, msg_req);
+    }
+
+    return virtio_msg_bus_send(bus, msg_req);
+}
+
 static void virtio_msg_bus_class_init(ObjectClass *klass, const void *data)
 {
     BusClass *bc = BUS_CLASS(klass);
